  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}+2x+15<0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}+2x+15\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/990d3828c9cf09da563aa59158afe6eafcb02635770de1a54029877d8f0a6f27.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-3$ or $x>5.$",
